# Exclude host build output from the Docker build context.
#
# Why this file exists: the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` had no filter, so every host `bin/` and `obj/` tree was
# uploaded into the build context and merged into the image's source directory before `dotnet publish`. Two
# concrete consequences, both of which this repository has already been bitten by in the *general* case
# (docs/STATE.md DEBT-11: emitted artifacts shadowing real inputs):
#
#   1. The build is no longer a clean-room build. A stale `obj/project.assets.json` produced by a different
#      SDK/NuGet version on a laptop can resolve differently than CI, which is the exact class of failure
#      Central Package Management exists to prevent (api/Directory.Packages.props, DECISION-m3-backend-api-003).
#   2. The context is tens of megabytes larger, and BuildKit transfers it on every build.
#
# `tests/` is excluded because the image publishes only src/JobTracker.Api; the test project is a
# *verification* artifact, and it is also where the largest host-built binaries live.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.user
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
tests/
docker-compose.yml
README.md
dotnet-tools.json
